      "slug": "boxy-fit-g112",
      "term": "Boxy fit",
      "definition": "A garment cut with straight sides and no waist shaping. The back and fronts are worked as rectangles with the same stitch count from hem to armhole. The shape sits squarely at the hip without tapering."
    },
    {
      "slug": "dc-collar-g112",
      "term": "DC collar",
      "definition": "A stand-up collar worked by picking up stitches around the back neck and front neck edges, then working rows of dc outward for 6 to 8 cm. The collar sits away from the neck rather than lying flat."
    },
    {
      "slug": "dc2tog-g112",
      "term": "Dc2tog",
      "definition": "Double crochet two stitches together. Used at the inner neck edge of each front half to shape the V-neck opening."
    }
  ],
